Package: latex2grad
Type: Package
Title: Verifiable Differentiation of Formulas Written in LaTeX
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Che", "Cheng", email = "lufee2005@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: End-to-end, verifiable differentiation of formulas written in
    LaTeX (or captured as images). A deterministic grammar parses LaTeX into
    an R expression tree and records every reading it had to choose; the
    tree is normalized to a canonical form and differentiated symbolically
    through 'DefDiff' (gradient, Hessian, Jacobian). Terms outside DefDiff's
    language are named in the report and handled by closed-form rules or
    numerically. Every result carries a certificate: a parse/print round
    trip and a comparison with Richardson-extrapolated central differences
    at random points. Reports are written as LaTeX, Markdown, or text. An
    optional language model may be used at the entry only, to transcribe an
    image or to resolve ambiguous notation, and each of its decisions is
    written into the report.
